body:
This PR addresses #10694 by introducing `invertInDarkMode` on `BinaryFileData` and the `invertSVGInDarkMode` App property. `invertSVGInDarkMode` defaults to true.

**Rational:**
`invertInDarkMode` allows the flexibility for the host app to set some images to be inverted (e.g. embedded PDF pages rendered as bitmaps) and others not (e.g. photos). I believe the default setting of true for SVGs is the right choice, however, we can change the default to false. If the default is changed to false, then I recommend adding mermaid diagrams that are rendered as SVGs (i.e. those unsupported yet by mermaidToExcalidraw such as state diagrams) with binaryFile.invertInDarkMode = true;

fixes: #10422
